hadiths[15]{hadithnumber,text}:
"575","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that` the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed (at a place) for nineteen days and continued to shorten the prayers throughout."
"576","Narrated Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): We traveled with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Madinah to Makkah, and he continued to pray two rak‘ahs (for each prayer) until we returned to Madinah. (The narrator Abu Ishaq said:) I asked (Anas, may Allah be pleased with him): Did you stay in Makkah for some days? He said: Yes, we stayed there for ten days."
"577","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): I offered two rak'ahs of prayer in Mina along with the Prophet (peace be upon him), Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and also with the Commander of the Faithful, Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), during the early period of his caliphate (I also prayed two rak'ahs). After that, he started offering the full prayer."
"578","Haritha bin Wahb (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) led us in a two-unit prayer at Mina during a time of complete peace."
"579","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): When it was said to him that Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) led us in four rak'ahs of prayer at Mina, he said, ""Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un."" Then he said, ""I performed two rak'ahs at Mina with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I performed two rak'ahs at Mina with Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), and I performed two rak'ahs at Mina with Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). Would that, instead of these four rak'ahs, I had those two accepted rak'ahs (which the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to perform)."
"580","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a distance of one day and night unless she is accompanied by a mahram."
"581","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he was in a hurry during a journey, he would delay the Maghrib prayer, then when he performed it, he would pray three rak'ahs, and after waiting for a short while, he would perform the Isha prayer and pray two rak'ahs, then he would say salam. And after Isha, he would not pray any voluntary prayer until he got up at midnight and performed the Tahajjud prayer."
"582","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to offer voluntary prayers while riding, even though he would be heading in a direction other than the Qiblah."
"583","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he offered prayer while riding a donkey and his face was towards the left of the Qiblah. (When he finished the prayer) he was asked, ""You prayed against the direction of the Qiblah?"" He replied, ""If I had not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing so, I would never have done it."
"584","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` I have accompanied the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) (on many journeys), but I have never seen him offering Sunnah prayers during travel, and Allah Almighty (in Surah Al-Mumtahina) says that ""Indeed, in the actions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) there is a best example for you."
"585","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Amir bin Rabi’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing voluntary prayers at night while traveling on his mount, regardless of which direction the mount was facing (even if it was not facing the Ka’bah)."
"586","Narrated Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them): When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling, he would combine the Zuhr and Asr prayers, and he would also combine and perform the Maghrib and Isha prayers together."
"587","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I had hemorrhoids, so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about prayer—whether it is permissible to pray while sitting. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Pray standing, and if you are not able, then sitting, and if you are not able to sit, then lie on your side and pray."
"588","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that she never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performing the Tahajjud prayer sitting down, until when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) became older, he would recite (Qur'an) while sitting, and then when he intended to bow (for ruku'), he would stand up and recite about thirty or forty verses and then perform ruku'."
"589","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says in a narration that he used to do the same in the second rak'ah as well. Then when the Prophet (peace be upon him) completed the prayer, he would see: if I was awake, he would talk with me, and if I was asleep, the Prophet (peace be upon him) would remain lying down."
